{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1382598-the-swoon-alembic","id":1382598,"title":"The Swoon Alembic","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-19T14:38:05-07:00","id":1382598,"title":"The Swoon Alembic","content":"Hi,<br /> <br /> I'm running a mixed game with one player as a Created.<br /> <br /> I do however keep running into an issue during action scenes or tense scenes with the Swoon Alembic (Core, pg.145). This is a roll of 3 sources minus 1 fixed stat, a single success knocks them unconscious.<br /> <br /> This basically plays out as, once per round one opponent is eliminated as a threat. There is no reasonable way that a character who is putting XP/stats behind their powers is going to be failing that roll.<br /> <br /> This has obvious issues in fights with a central figure/threat but also in all sorts of action scenes or tense scenes like a chase scene (just knock them out) or an infiltration scene (the guard blocking the way? Not anymore) etc.<br /> <br /> It's not unique in its ability to 'one shot' a threat. A Mage can cast a spell to incapacitate a target. The Vampire could Dominate them, etc. but this one feels more...egregious because it seem there's nothing the target can do to meaningfully resist beyond 'have had a backstory that caused you to have a very high Stamina stat'.<br /> <br /> How do you GMs deal with these kind of powers or abilities that shut down entire classes of threats/types of scene?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T16:33:12-07:00","id":1382632,"title":"","content":"Swoon costs three Pyros to prime and has a range of three yards per Azoth. Many characters can run far enough away for that to be a non-issue in a turn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T07:05:39-07:00","id":1382745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1382598-the-swoon-alembic?p=1382632#post1382632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Swoon costs three Pyros to prime and has a range of three yards per Azoth. Many characters can run far enough away for that to be a non-issue in a turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming that the PC hasn't gone into the encounter with it charged already and that the targets know they have that power and would know to stand 3*Azoth yards away. And if someone randomly falls unconscious after a brief shriek of terror the uneducated probably don't immediately assume that the real threat is the PC.<br /> <br /> My assumption was that most things in setting are not well informed on the abilities of the Created power set and so would not really be...pre-prepared to deal with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T07:23:59-07:00","id":1382747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1382598-the-swoon-alembic?p=1382745#post1382745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming that the PC hasn't gone into the encounter with it charged already and that the targets know they have that power and would know to stand 3*Azoth yards away.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the capstone power of an Alembic that makes you better at being scary. Literally all of the powers in the Alembic key off of Intimidation and the one you get for free makes it easier to render people momentarily ineffective by completely mundane means.<br /> <br /> Swoon costs at least a third of the Pyros capacity of a Promethean that isn't capable of consistent superhuman Traits and Prometheans are normally incentivized to keep their effective Azoth rating low because &quot;spending a lot of Pyros&quot; is a trigger condition for half their drawbacks.<br /> <br /> You should probably expect a character who is good at being scary and throwing all of their weight behind it to be able to push through mortal-level threats at close range in a scene where they're going loud.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And if someone randomly falls unconscious after a brief shriek of terror the uneducated probably don't immediately assume that the real threat is the PC. </div> </div> </div>If someone is a mortal then they're reasonably below the pay-grade for casually resisting a knockout power. If someone is immune to being knocked out (and the game has many antagonists who fit that bill) then it's reasonable to conclude that a power whose method of resistance is built for damage reduction doesn't automatically knock them out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My assumption was that most things in setting are not well informed on the abilities of the Created power set and so would not really be...pre-prepared to deal with them. </div> </div> </div>My assumption is that Prometheans are incentivized to use big bursts of Azothic power sparingly because the game has consequences for doing so. Use threats that don't have mortal biology or use threats that have guns or secondary actors that work for them long enough to let them force a scene-change. Pyros takes time to recover.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":".  Typos. 04-20-2020, 11:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T04:37:15-07:00","id":1382953,"title":"","content":"Interesting, I may need the player to walk me through Azoth, Pyros and their power stat again (I am juggling 6 splats worth of stuff so am leaving the finer details to the players). From what I've understood so long as they can plug themselves into a power source they're able to keep charged up with Pyros and in a modern city that's not much of a challenge.<br /> <br /> Not all threats are mortals. I am not arguing that a mortal should be able to resist a top end supernatural power. I am rather more concerned about things like animal monstrosities some mad-creator has thrown at them (why would an amalgam of animals be immune to unconsciousness? It has an organic body and the like), Changelings and other supernatural creatures that run off a more human biology, etc.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T14:12:22-07:00","id":1383034,"title":"","content":"Yes, Prometheans can replenish Pyros from contact with dangerous levels of electricity. Thing is, the amount of time they can draw from a given power source before risking shorting it out entirely is measured in turns and depends on how strong a source of electricity it is. They can't just replenish to full off any wall socket, basically.<br /> They do have other ways to gain Pyros, granted (interacting with mortals for a while, sleeping near meaningful quantities of their element, encountering a thunderstorm, the sun rising), so it's not exactly the hardest fuel stat to keep topped off among supernatural critters, but it's not <i>that</i> easy. And, yeah, there's the whole &quot;spending Pyros can cause Disquiet in witnesses and (if enough is spent) <i>create or worsen Wastelands</i>&quot; thing. So, uh... yeah, most Prometheans probably shouldn't be just tossing it around very lightly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T18:22:30-07:00","id":1383061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1382598-the-swoon-alembic?p=1382953#post1382953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting, I may need the player to walk me through Azoth, Pyros and their power stat again (I am juggling 6 splats worth of stuff so am leaving the finer details to the players). From what I've understood so long as they can plug themselves into a power source they're able to keep charged up with Pyros and in a modern city that's not much of a challenge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless you're dealing with big stuff like power stations and train lines, most casually-accessible sources of electricity will short out after a couple of turns; meanwhile, pretty much every other source of Pyros is a drip feed or requires time at the scale of hours to generate.<br /> <br /> Azoth affects how likely you are to inflict Disquiet, how quickly your Wastelands form and how far they spread, how far away your presence awakens Pandorans from, and how likely you are to succumb to Torment. You can choose to reduce it to a lower effective rating, but (without making use of a location-bound Merit) doing so means you're locked into that rating for at least a day, and returning to a higher rating doesn't refill your Pyros pool on its own; if you're familiar with Demon, think of it like going loud but in reverse \u2014 you have to build up the rating to be able to pull it out of your back pocket and you need to fill the extra capacity on your own, but if you've got the right Transmutations for the job then you're going to be extremely effective.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not all threats are mortals. I am not arguing that a mortal should be able to resist a top end supernatural power. I am rather more concerned about things like animal monstrosities some mad-creator has thrown at them (why would an amalgam of animals be immune to unconsciousness? It has an organic body and the like), Changelings and other supernatural creatures that run off a more human biology, etc. </div> </div> </div>There are many ways for characters to be immune to unconsciousness. Pretty much everything in the franchise that can be described as &quot;undead&quot; is, as are Prometheans, Pandorans, and clones (including animal hybrids); anything that heals bashing damage at an accelerated rate likewise reduces the interval for which the knockout lasts, including werewolves, mummies (albeit this is redundant with the preceding &quot;pretty much everything that can be described as undead&quot; point), some Beasts (whether fully-templated or the remains of one that's undergone the Merger), and some Deviants (or Manticores); and Hunter's got a core Tactic whose effects are &quot;everyone who participates in this Tactic gets a bonus to their Resistance traits against mundane or supernatural attempts to instill fear or doubt and can't be knocked out from bashing damage.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;This thing stays awake in the face of physical/mental trauma&quot; is a quality that very seldom needs extensive justification when dealing with supernatural weirdness. (Also, to turn your question around, why would an amalgam of animals be vulnerable to an ability that is part of a powerset premised on affecting human minds? What Integrity is going to be imperiled by the breaking point the power applies to it?)<br /> <br /> Getting access to this power involves at least a bit of time in the philosophic frameworks of either blending in among humanity or purging spiritual weaknesses, and keeping the power outside of those frameworks necessitates spending a limited resource (that you could instead use to buy Pilgrimage or Azoth) on becoming good at terrifying people for the rest of your character's existence; using any of the powers without looking like an obviously inhuman being and risking Disquiet necessitates becoming worse at Empathy until you deliberately fail a Social roll with a human being. This isn't a power that exists without contextual grounding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}